keel's rules for [1mscratch[22m [38;2;154;149;140m(saved in .keel/config.yml and .keel/rules/)[39m:

[1m[38;2;164;139;255mEngines:[39m[22m
  [1mclaude[22m: every edit, shell command, read and MCP call is checked before it runs
  [1mopencode[22m: every edit, shell command, read and MCP call is checked before it runs
  [1mcodex[22m: every edit, shell command, read and MCP call is checked before it runs
  [1mcopilot[22m: shell commands of git, gh, the package managers and file printers are checked before they
 run; file edits are checked after each step (the diff guard puts a refused file back)
  [1mapi[22m: every edit, shell command, read and MCP call is checked before it runs

[1m[38;2;164;139;255mAlways on:[39m[22m
  [38;2;195;166;255mphase-matrix[39m: Each phase lets agents change only some kinds of files: tests in RED, code in GREEN,
 nothing in a review. [38;2;154;149;140m(in a flow)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255menv-files[39m: .env files hold secrets: agents never read, print or change them (setup may write the
env file). [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mkeel-rules-files[39m: Agents never change .keel/config.yml or .keel/rules/: an agent may not change
its own rules. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mkeel-keys[39m: keel's own keys (its internal token and the sign-in key) are never read, printed,
changed or sent by an agent: with them anyone could act as keel or as you. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mmigrations-immutable[39m: An existing database migration is never changed; a new migration file is
added instead. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mforce-push[39m: git push --force and git push -f are refused: they can delete other people's work.
[38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mno-verify[39m: --no-verify is refused: it skips the checks keel relies on. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mcommit-in-flow[39m: In a flow keel makes every commit after its checks; an agent's own git commit is
refused. [38;2;154;149;140m(in a flow)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mhistory-rewrite[39m: git reset --hard and git rebase -i are refused in a flow: they throw work away.
[38;2;154;149;140m(in a flow)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255msecrets-at-write[39m: An edit that adds what looks like a secret (a key, a token, a password) is
refused before it is written. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mdisabled-tests[39m: A test may not be switched off: skip, only, @Disabled, xit and the like are
refused in test files. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m

[1m[38;2;164;139;255mkeel's rules you can switch off:[39m[22m
  [38;2;195;166;255mgenerated[39m: Generated files are not edited by hand: change the source and run the generator.
[38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mread-build-output[39m: Build output (build/, node_modules/, target/ ...) is not read: it wastes the
agent's context. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mskip-test-flags[39m: -x test and -x check are refused: they skip the tests in a Gradle build. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mnew-dependency[39m: Installing a new package is a decision for the spec and a gate, not for an agent.
[38;2;154;149;140m(in a flow)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mread-twice[39m: Reading the same unchanged file twice in one step is refused: the agent already has
it. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mbig-file-read[39m: A big file (more lines than read_guard_max_lines) is read in parts, with offset and
 limit. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mpush-gate[39m: An agent's git push or gh pr create is refused while keel's push blockers say the
branch is not ready. [38;2;154;149;140m(always)[39m
  [38;2;195;166;255mmcp-writes[39m: In a flow, an MCP tool that can change things runs only when mcp.allow names it. [38;2;154;149;140m(in a[39m
 flow)

